{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion","id":27026,"title":"Stopgap Werewolf: the Forsaken GMC conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T23:29:20-08:00","id":27026,"title":"Stopgap Werewolf: the Forsaken GMC conversion","content":"I'm reposting this from the old forums since there don't seem to be any other stopgap conversions that made the jump. As always, feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Werewolf: the Forsaken </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">God Machine Chronicle Update</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I borrowed some of the Uratha form changes from Pendragon, a poster on the Onyx Path forums.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Two of the new conditions are from the Blood and Smoke: Reap the Whirlwind quickstart. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Character Creation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Werewolves receive 10 merit points at character creation. The fifth dot of a trait does not cost two points.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Use the Virtue and Vice system from the GMC book. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Experience</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Attribute</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merit</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Totem</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skill Specialty</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skill</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Affinity Gift</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:: 3 Experiences per gift</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other Gift</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per gift</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Primary Renown</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other Renown</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Harmony</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Primal Urge</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rites</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Willpower</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Harmony</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Having seen the way Humanity is handled in Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, I have decided to leave Harmony as it is in the W:tF core rulebook, except instead of derangements, I will be adding custom conditions for Harmony rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Roll Results</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character\u2019s world view has been damaged, perhaps beyond repair. The character suffers from traumatic stress. Lose a dot of Harmony and choose from the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Broken, Fugue, or Spiritual Obsession. Also, take a Beat.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character\u2019s world view has been shaken and he probably questions his sense of self, his ability to relate to people, his own moral worth, or his sanity. Lose a dot of Harmony and choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Bestial, or Competitive.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The character has come through the breaking point intact. He might feel guilty or upset about what happened, but he can cope. Choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Bestial, or Competitive.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:The character somehow manages not only to survive the breaking point, but to find meaning in it, to reaffirm his own self-worth, or to pass through fire and become tempered by it. The character takes a Beat and regains a point of Willpower.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Harmony Conditions</span></b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Bestial </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Your character acts on primal, physical impulses. Frightening things make him run. He meets aggressive threats with violence and anger. Take -2 to all rolls to resist frenzy or physical impulse. As well, take -2 to Defense due to impulsive action. Any rolls to compel your character to impulsive, aggressive action or escape achieve exceptional success on three successes instead of five. This could apply to Disciplines such as Nightmare, or Dominate under the right circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resolution: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Take an action during a frenzy that results in a breaking point. This Condition fades naturally after a number of days equal to your Primal Urge. After resolving Bestial, your character cannot be subject to this Condition again for a full month.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Beat: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">n/a</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Competitive </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Your character must assert dominance and superiority. Either she gives it her all, or she falters. Any time she\u2019s in direct competition with another character, she suffers -2 on any rolls where she doesn\u2019t spend Willpower. This includes contested rolls. As well, any rolls to tempt or coerce her into competition achieve exceptional success on three successes instead of five.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common Causes</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: A challenging predatory aura conflict, or a failed Detachment roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resolution</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Win or lose a competition where someone reaches a breaking point. This Condition fades naturally after a number of days equal to your Primal Urge. After resolving Competitive, your character cannot be subject to this Condition again for a full month.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Beat</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: n/a</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Spiritual Obsession</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The character gains a ban or compulsion as described on pages 185-186 of Werewolf: the Forsaken. She gains the 9-again quality on all rolls related to pursuing her obsession. On rolls that are unrelated to her obsession, she loses the 10-again quality. Obsession can be a temporary or persistent quality per Storyteller approval. Depending on the nature of the compulsion, the character may take a -2 on some social interactions. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Resolution</i>: The character sheds or purges her fixation by reaffirming her connection to humanity as a counterweight to her spiritual side.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Beat</i>: Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her obsession.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Shadows Into Light\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Uratha Forms</span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hishu (The Human): +2 to perception rolls.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dalu (The Near-Human): Strength +1, Stamina +1, Manipulation \u20131, Size +1, Health +2, Speed +1, +2 to perception rolls. 9-again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Can deal lethal damage unarmed.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gauru (The Wolfman): Rage invoked, Strength +3, Dexterity +1, Stamina +2, Size +2, Health +4, Initiative +1, Speed +4, Armor 1/1, inflict lethal damage (+1 bonus to claw attacks, +2 to bite attacks), +3 to perception rolls, wound penalties ignored and no unconsciousness rolls made, \u20132 to resist Death Rage, fail most Social and Mental tasks. 8 again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Urshul (The Near-Wolf): Strength +2, Dexterity +2, Stamina +2, Manipulation \u20133, Size +1, Health +3, Initiative +2, Speed +7, +3 to perception rolls, inflict lethal damage, 9-again on all Strength and brawl rolls. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Urhan (The Wolf): Dexterity +2, Stamina +1, Size \u20131, Initiative +2, Speed +5, +4 to perception rolls, inflict lethal damage with bite attack. Use (the higher of Dex or Wits) + Athletics to determine defense.</span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 12-10-2013, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T02:00:31-08:00","id":27840,"title":"","content":"First impression: That's a LOT of experience for Renowns; I'm not completely sure but is anything 5 Experiences per dot in the new system? Even attributes are 4 per.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T03:01:27-08:00","id":27858,"title":"","content":"Power Stat is 5xp per dot. As Renown and Primal Urge had the same x8 multiplier they both defaulted to 5xp apiece. But Renown was awful expensive before too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:27:42-08:00","id":27886,"title":"","content":"Furthermore when you buy a dot of Renown you gain a free Gift, so essentially Primary Renown is only 1 XP and Other Renown is 2 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:10:48-08:00","id":27983,"title":"","content":"Renown is awfully expensive. In the original core, it's<br /> Primary (Auspice, Tribe) Renown = new dots x 6.<br /> Other Renown = new dots x 8.<br /> <br /> I also think that Gifts might be too expensive in the light of the fact that in Demon, embeds and exploits (discrete powers which seem more like Gifts than Disciplines or Arcana) cost 2 experiences each. I need to read through Gifts to see if they're actually worth 3 and 4 experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:53:36-08:00","id":28007,"title":"","content":"I for one, can't wait till they fix gift linearity, and cheapen them up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:48:27-08:00","id":28782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion?p=28007#post28007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, can't wait till they fix gift linearity, and cheapen them up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, coming in mid-conversation....<br /> <br /> You want them more linear or less?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T12:23:54-08:00","id":28875,"title":"","content":"Could be either. Right now, they're confusing. There's an order to them, but you can buy them out of order with extra xp costs in the old system. Also, buying a point of renown gives you a free gift, even if it's out of order. <br /> <br /> For the purposes of my conversion, maximum gift rating cannot exceed highest primary renown, but all gift costs are normalized. 1 dot gift costs as much as a 5 dot gift, and they do not have to be purchased in order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:11:54-08:00","id":28919,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's why I was asking. More linear would be nice to tighten it up and they could add more Gift lists to cover the ones that get squeezed out. Less linear and it's a nice free-for-all. Get what you can when you can.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyone remember if the Apocalypse Gifts were like that? Free-for-all, tiered XP rate? I've got it stuck in my head it was, but I didn't play it much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-12-2013, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T17:08:02-08:00","id":29014,"title":"","content":"I love All Good Gifts. Does that answers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:39:43-08:00","id":29337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion?p=29014#post29014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love All Good Gifts. Does that answers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:50:53-08:00","id":48163,"title":"","content":"Octavo, have you made any updates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:23:04-08:00","id":48228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion?p=48163#post48163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Octavo, have you made any updates?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering changing the gift costs to 2 (base) + 1 (for non affinity) + 1 (if gift is purchased out of order.) I'm not sure whether gifts should be as expensive as B&amp;S Disciplines or Mage Arcana. They seem more like Demon embeds and exploits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T20:22:49-08:00","id":52107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion?p=28919#post28919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's why I was asking. More linear would be nice to tighten it up and they could add more Gift lists to cover the ones that get squeezed out. Less linear and it's a nice free-for-all. Get what you can when you can.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyone remember if the Apocalypse Gifts were like that? Free-for-all, tiered XP rate? I've got it stuck in my head it was, but I didn't play it much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda.<br /> Apocalypse's Gift system has them rated at level 1 to 5 (6, if you're suitably epic), with each level costing more than the last, but there are no prerequisites, no surcharge for purchasing out of order (since there is no order, just a collection of Gifts along a broad theme), and since Renown doesn't cost XP (but is RP dependent), it doesn't become so much of a tax. They *are* sorted into lists by Tribe, Auspice and Breed, with Gifts from the groups you belong to being less expensive (by a bunch) and easier to obtain (by more than a bunch) than others.<br /> That said, they're all still pretty cheap (until level 4 and 5, anyway, but those tend to be terrifically powerful in application). Less than Vampire Disciplines (you can basically pick up two level one Gifts for a Vampires 1 Discipline dot).<br /> <br /> I tried to avoid posting numbers because I thought it would make it too complicated, but I feel I have achieved the opposite. Hell and damnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}